+{"id":"README-7","title":"P4 — README HTTP API curl examples (L323-335) have the API-key header inside the quoted URL: -H \"X-API-Key: *** \"http://... — as written the header arg is consumed as part of one quoted token, so the documented commands do not run correctly","priority":"P4","status":"pending","created_at":"2026-10-04T15:20:00Z","created_by":"duckbrain-readme lane 2026-10-04","complexity":1,"type":"accuracy","reasoning":"README audit 2026-10-04 (readme lane tick duckbrain-readme-2026-10-04-15-09-42), truth check, README.md bbee2cc 2026-09-30. Lines 323, 326, 329, 332 and 335 all read: curl -H \"X-API-Key: *** \"http://localhost:3000/api/...\" — the closing double-quote after *** terminates the -H argument and the URL opens its own quote with no space before it, so the shell passes -H 'X-API-Key: *** \"http://localhost:3000/api/keys?namespace=default\"' as ONE argument (verified byte-exact with cat -A). Net effect: no URL argument and a garbage header — curl errors out. FIX: close the header quote before the URL, e.g. curl -H \"X-API-Key: *** http://localhost:3000/api/keys?namespace=default\" (space between *** and URL) on all five lines 323/326/329/332/335. Note: doc severity P4 by ruling 2026-09-30; do not re-raise.","detail":{"fingerprint":"readme7-curl-quote-2026-10-04"},"evidence":"sed -n '323p' README.md | cat -A -> curl -H \"X-API-Key: *** \"http://localhost:3000/api/keys?namespace=default\"$ (same shape on 326/329/332/335). Control: README quickstart block (L113-131) executed live against port 3777 on 2026-10-04 — namespace create 200, memory write returned id 898bdef7, read-back returned content 'first memory from the quickstart' (quickstart itself is correct).","files_changed":["README.md"]}
+{"id":"README-8","title":"P4 — README's duckbrain CLI commands (consolidate/embeddings/s3/ssh-*) are never made runnable: the repo's install path (git clone + pnpm install) does NOT put a duckbrain binary on PATH or even in node_modules/.bin","priority":"P4","status":"pending","created_at":"2026-10-04T15:20:00Z","created_by":"duckbrain-readme lane 2026-10-04","complexity":2,"type":"install-path","reasoning":"README audit 2026-10-04, install-path check on README.md bbee2cc. The README Quick Start documents only pnpm install (L101) and pnpm start ..., but L173-174 (duckbrain consolidate), L356-361 (duckbrain embeddings status/rebuild/install-hooks/providers), L207-209 (duckbrain s3 status/sync/query) and L182-184 (duckbrain ssh-test/ssh-connect) all invoke a bare duckbrain command as if globally installed. Measured 2026-10-04 on this repo after pnpm install: which duckbrain -> not found; ls node_modules/.bin/duckbrain -> No such file or directory (package.json declares bin duckbrain->./bin/duckbrain.js but pnpm did not link it at the root); pnpm exec duckbrain --version -> ERR_PNPM_RECURSIVE_EXEC_FIRST_FAIL 'Command duckbrain not found'. A stranger who follows the README cannot run any of the documented CLI sections. FIX: add one line after the install block telling readers how to get the binary — e.g. pnpm link --global (or npm i -g .), or change the documented commands to pnpm exec duckbrain ... / node bin/duckbrain.js ..., whichever the maintainer prefers; verify the chosen form on a fresh clone. Doc severity P4 by ruling 2026-09-30; do not re-raise.","detail":{"fingerprint":"readme8-duckbrain-bin-2026-10-04"},"evidence":"which duckbrain -> empty; ls node_modules/.bin/duckbrain -> 'No such file or directory'; pnpm exec duckbrain --version -> 'Command duckbrain not found' (all run 2026-10-04 in /home/kara/duckbrain @ bbee2cc, node_modules present). Control: node bin/duckbrain.js --help works and lists consolidate/embeddings/s3/ssh-test, so the commands exist — only the PATH story is missing.","files_changed":["README.md"]}
